"@context": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/context/v1"
"@id": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/decision-0002-streams"
"@type": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/ontology/Decision"
label: "ADR 0002: streams — append-only event logs on AtomicKeyspace"
timestamp: "2026-08-21T10:51:16"
source: "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/path/docs/decisions/0002-streams.md"
requires: "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/decision-0001-atomic-keyspace"
references:
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-kernel-extension"
  - "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-13-state"
statement: >
  The streams crate: per-stream append-only event logs as immutable,
  individually addressable objects at streams/v1/<id>/log/<seq:020>
  under the kernel keyspace root. Chosen: the event object's
  conditional create IS the seq allocation — no counter, no head CAS;
  byte-identical retries are idempotent only inside the bounded
  pre-scan window (beyond it, same-stable-id re-appends land as new
  events: at-least-once, consumers dedupe by event id; in-window
  payload/schema change is a typed IdempotencyConflict, never a
  silent second landing); complete=true requires BOTH a verified tail
  hint (a computed-key GET witness a frozen LIST cannot hide) AND an
  empty ordered probe — a LIST alone never certifies (G130); reads
  are typed and loud (Corrupt names missing seqs, decode failure is
  an error never a skip, OffsetExpired is the typed trim boundary),
  and a backend failing the strong-LIST contract yields
  BackendUnqualified rather than false completeness. Certified trim
  (batch 5): immutable trims/ certificates are the floor, GC deletes
  only below it, trim-to-end is logically empty with appends landing
  AT the floor (finding D). Quiesced migration from the ADR-0011
  layout preserves seqs/payloads and seals each migrated stream —
  the seal is the tail-erasure witness. Rejected: the ADR-0011
  single-lineage event stream (all repos serialize through one head
  CAS, O(history) replay, lineage-wide damage); unfenced trim
  (unblocked only by 0001's versioned values); mode-A/mode-B fencing
  designs (reserved, not shipped); per-event tombstones; and for the
  crate itself, delivery/push/bus, forge types, and name registries —
  pull-only, opaque ids, the application maps names at its boundary.
  Flips if: retention needs grow past certified trim (a future
  fenced-retirement decision) or 0001's era model is superseded.
